# Prettier is deliberately not allowed to reformat these four files.
#
# Each one contains a line whose exact shape is copied into the emitted
# JavaScript by TypeScript's printer, so reformatting it changes `dist/`:
#
#   announcement/announcement.module.ts
#       The `imports: [...]` array. Left inline, TypeScript emits it on one
#       line; broken up, it emits one element per line. This is the only case
#       where formatting changes the compiled bytes.
#
#   announcement/announcement.service.ts
#   bot-provider/bot-provider.ts
#       Statement layout pinned token-by-token by the runtime source maps
#       (a blank line inside getNightlyClosureCronExpression; a 96-column
#       sendMessageTmp signature the original kept unwrapped).
#
#   database-provider/prisma.service.ts
#       An 88-column class header with two `implements` clauses, which the
#       original likewise left unwrapped.
#
# These are the only places where the recovered source departs from the
# `.prettierrc` style, and they are what keep the build byte-identical to the
# runtime snapshot. Re-run ./scripts/verify-against-snapshot.sh before removing
# an entry here. See docs/RECONSTRUCTION.md sections 3 and 4.

